      "title": "FICO Q4 Earnings Beat on Scores, Pricing and Software Growth",
      "summary": "Fair Isaac (FICO) reported Q4 FY2026 non-GAAP earnings of $11.10 per share, up 43.4% YoY and beating consensus estimates. Revenues grew 27.4% to $657.05 million, driven by higher mortgage origination score pricing and strong software platform growth. Software ARR reached $851 million with platform ARR up 72%. However, management withheld FY2027 guidance citing uncertainty around mortgage pricing transitions and continued weakness in mortgage market activity due to elevated interest rates.",
